# ssh-keygen -Y verify -f (see "ALLOWED SIGNERS" in ssh-keygen(1)).
# docs/verifying-releases.md says how to use this file. Keep a replaced key listed,
# so that older releases still verify, unless it was compromised. A key added for
# releases made through the broker uses the identity warden-release, which is what
# scripts/sign-release.sh and docs/verifying-releases.md check against. The older
# line below keeps its own identity and verifies the releases signed before that.
